# Drafted by Gemini (R22 n2), edited.

~ wood_start
Narrator: Autumn beech and hickory crowd under a swollen full moon, their dark bark stamped with ghost-white handprints every fifteen feet.
quest crooked_nightmare dark_wood
* [Perception DC 15] Listen for the loudest crying -> found | notfound
* [Survival DC 15] Read the handprint trail -> found | notfound
* Follow the handprint trees for ten minutes -> trail
* Look around -> END

~ found
Narrator: A thin, hiccuping sob cuts through the rustle of dry leaves, leading straight toward a moonlit hollow.
set nm_wood_direction
-> END

~ notfound
Narrator: The wind rattles the hickory hulls until every branch sounds like a weeping child. The chalky handprints on the trunks still point the way forward.
-> END

~ trail
Narrator: Ten minutes of cold leaf-mold and pale little palms bring you to a clearing where the moonlight pools like milk.
time +10
set nm_wood_direction
-> END

~ child_start
Narrator: A little girl in a white dress shivers in the grass, clutching a one-eyed stuffed doll stitched together like half turkey and half lizard.
nm_adela_child [afraid]: Please do not walk so loud, the trees have ears tonight. Poor Frederick is so terribly hungry, and I have nothing left to feed him.
set nm_child_met
* Comfort her -> comfort
* Ask about the doll -> doll
* [if item:nm_wicker_star] Hold up the wicker star -> star_used
* Ask for the doll -> frederick_wakes
* Leave her be -> END

~ comfort
Narrator: Her small shoulders stop trembling at your gentle word, and the moonlight catches a dark mole on her right cheek.
nm_adela_child [sad]: You sound like the warm kitchen downstairs. I thought everyone had gone and left me in the dark.
set nm_child_comforted
-> child_start

~ doll
nm_adela_child [afraid]: Nurse stitched him from scraps so I would not be lonely. When the dark comes close and he gets frightened, he gobbles up whatever he can reach.
-> child_start

~ frederick_wakes
Narrator: The burlap seams split with a wet rip as the doll balloons into a feathered hulk, its button eye glaring above a beak full of jagged teeth.
quest frederick_the_turkey found
combat nm_frederick

~ star_used
Narrator: The doll swells with a hiss of dry stuffing, then catches sight of the woven straw star in `{name}`'s hand. With an offended squawk, the beastly thing backs off ten feet and shrinks back into a limp lump of cloth.
quest frederick_the_turkey found
set nm_frederick_done
set frederick_repelled
xp fight nm_frederick
-> frederick_toy

~ frederick_toy
Narrator: Frederick lies among the fallen beech leaves, staring up at the moon with his single button eye.
* Take Frederick with you -> take
* Tuck Frederick back into Adela's arms -> bed
* Leave him in the leaves -> left
* Do nothing yet -> END

~ take
Narrator: You tuck the ragged doll into your pack, where his stitched beak gives a faint, rhythmic chew against the leather.
give frederick_corn_dolly
set frederick_taken
quest frederick_the_turkey kept
-> stonoga

~ bed
Narrator: Little Adela gathers the ragged creature against her chest, lets out a long sigh, and falls asleep standing up.
set frederick_in_bed
quest frederick_the_turkey bed
-> stonoga

~ left
Narrator: You leave the stuffed creature in the damp leaves. Behind you, a tiny beak gives a single, hollow click.
set frederick_left
quest frederick_the_turkey left
-> stonoga

~ stonoga
Narrator: Stonoga Blackstinger steps from the tree line in a tall white chef's hat, her hundred little legs pattering under a flour-dusted apron. Before you can reach the child, unseen hands yank the girl in the white dress backward into the dark trees.
cutscene nm_three_adelas_a
set nm_wood_done
quest crooked_nightmare crooked_oven
nm_stonoga [sly]: Golub prattles over the mind and Vessla fusses with the soul, as if a feast begins anywhere but the butcher's block! A tender vessel must be salted with fright and trussed up tight before the oven door ever opens.
* Strike the vision -> stonoga_hit
* Listen to her boast -> stonoga_boast
* Let her go -> END

~ stonoga_hit
Narrator: Your blow passes through her apron with a soft pop, leaving only a drift of warm baker's flour on the night air.
vanish nm_stonoga
set stonoga_struck
-> END

~ stonoga_boast
nm_stonoga [smile]: That is the secret my sisters never had the stomach for: fear makes the marrow sweet, and the little lady has been simmering since she was knee-high! Come along into the kitchen, darlings, the coals are red.
Narrator: Across the clearing, the crooked door lying flat in the leaves begins to glow dull red around its edges.
-> END

~ door
if not flag.nm_wood_done
Narrator: The crooked door lies flat in the dead leaves, sealed fast, though the pale handprints pressed into the wood still feel warm to the touch.
-> END
else
Narrator: The handprint-covered door lies open to the red dark below, asking no toll at all.
* Step through -> pass
* [Performance DC 12] Tell the door a joke -> joke_ok | joke_fail
* Not yet -> END
endif

~ joke_ok
Narrator: A wooden giggle rattles through the hinges, and all the chalky little handprints wave at you in unison.
set dream_laughed
-> pass

~ joke_fail
Narrator: The door listens with the polite silence of well-seasoned oak and keeps its thoughts to itself.
-> pass

~ pass
quest crooked_nightmare crooked_oven
move nm_oven
